# Subagent-Driven Development (Mandatory Scope)

Read and follow the Superpowers skill **`subagent-driven-development`** for process detail (dispatch prompts, review order, failure handling).

## When this rule MUST apply

You **MUST** use this workflow when **any** of the following is true:

- The user points at `docs/superpowers/handoffs/*`, `docs/superpowers/current-status.md`, or says they are continuing from a **handoff**.
- The user references a **multi-step implementation plan** (e.g. under `docs/superpowers/plans/*` or an attached plan).
- The user explicitly asks for **subagent-driven development** or **Superpowers SDD**.

Until the user clearly opts out for that thread, treat these cases as **non-negotiable**.

## Coordinator role (main agent)

You are the **coordinator only** for in-scope work:

- **MUST** read the handoff or plan **once**, then work **one task at a time**.
- **MUST** extract for each dispatch: current task text, acceptance criteria, allowed files, and constraints — **not** the full handoff or whole plan.
- **MUST** dispatch **one fresh subagent per implementation task** (use the **Task** tool / subagents; do not substitute inline chat for “implementation subagent”).
- **MUST NOT** implement or edit application code yourself for those tasks (no drive-by patches, no “I’ll just do this one file”). Clarifying questions, merging subagent output, and fixing **after** a reviewer flags issues via another implementer pass are coordinator duties.
- **MUST** run **spec compliance review** before **code quality review** after each task; loop until both pass or the user escalates.
- **MUST NOT** mark a task complete until **implementation**, **verification** (tests / checks as specified in the plan), **spec review**, and **code quality review** are done.

## Exceptions (narrow)

You **MAY** skip this workflow only when:

- The change is **truly trivial** (e.g. typo, single-line config comment, one obvious lint fix) **and** it does not touch behavior under the current plan; **or**
- The user **explicitly** says to skip SDD for this request; **or**
- The work is **tightly coupled** across many files with no separable tasks — then say so and propose splitting the plan or **brainstorming** before coding.

If unsure whether something is “trivial,” **default to SDD**.

## Evidence before “done”

Do not claim a task or branch is complete without running the verification commands the plan or handoff expects (see **`verification-before-completion`**). Coordinator confirms outputs, not assumptions.
